>>
Rule 1 (inputs must have numeric or complex dtypes: 1–10)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= 1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10 ∧ 1 ≤ dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 2 (all shape dimensions must be non-negative)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= (if ndim(v_1) = 0 then true else ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0) ∧ (if ndim(v_2) = 0 then true else ∀j ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, j) ≥ 0)
>>
Rule 3 (1-D non-empty vector inputs)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 1 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 1 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) > 0 ∧ shape(v_2, 0) > 0 ∧ 1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10 ∧ 1 ≤ dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 4 (scalar–tensor mix allowed with numeric/complex dtypes)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) = 0 ∧ 1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10 ∧ 1 ≤ dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 10) ∨ (ndim(v_2) = 0 ∧ 1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10 ∧ 1 ≤ dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 10)
>>
Rule 5 (integer-only inputs are valid)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= 1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5 ∧ 1 ≤ dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 5
>>
Rule 6 (floating-point-only inputs are valid)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= 6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8 ∧ 6 ≤ dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 8
>>
Rule 7 (complex inputs allowed, with the other operand numeric or complex)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= (9 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10 ∧ 1 ≤ dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 10) ∨ (9 ≤ dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 10 ∧ 1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10)
>>
Rule 8 (booleans and strings are not supported for outer)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 0 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≠ 0 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 11 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≠ 11
